# Build context exclusions for `docker build` / `make docker-build`.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs pyproject.toml, src/, configs/, openapi.yaml and
# datasets/sec_fixtures_fy2024.json, so nothing else here can reach the image.
# It is still worth excluding: the daemon transfers the whole context before
# reading the Dockerfile, and .venv/ alone is 870 MB. refrence/ is listed
# because local reference material should not end up in a build context even
# transiently.

.git/
refrence/

.venv/
venv/
env/

.env
*.pem
*.key

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

tests/
docs/
terraform/
.github/
# `ui/` is deliberately NOT excluded. It used to be, on the grounds that
# Streamlit must not reach the runtime image - which is true, and is enforced
# where it belongs: the API Dockerfile simply does not COPY it. Excluding it
# from the shared build context instead broke `Dockerfile.ui`, which needs it.
# The directory is ~15KB; bounding context size was never the real motive.
